This code uses libgpiod to manage the GPIO lines, I2C communication, and logging. It takes 10 baseline samples, calculates the initial threshold, and then polls the reed sensor every 200 ms. If the distance reading drops below the threshold, it energizes the relay for 3 seconds, then de-energizes it and checks the reed sensor. If the reed sensor is LOW, it logs "door opened", otherwise "door not opened". The code also handles errors and cleans up resources on exit.

