This code uses the pigpio library to initialize the SPI interface, set the clock to 1 MHz, and set the SPI mode to single-ended. It then opens the log file in append mode and maps it to memory. The signal handler for SIGINT is set to close the log file, terminate pigpio, and exit cleanly.

The main loop reads the ADC value from the MCP3008, converts it to voltage, calculates PPM, logs the timestamp, voltage, and PPM to the log file, and prints the voltage and PPM to the console every second. If the ADC read fails, it retries up to three times with a 100 ms delay between retries.

