```

This code captures video from the CSI camera, exposes it as /dev/video0, and streams it over UDP to a target IP address and port given as command-line arguments. It uses V4L2 MMAP streaming with 4 buffers at 640x480 YUYV format, fragmenting each frame into UDP datagrams of at most 65000 bytes, each prefixed with a small header containing the frame index, fragment index, total fragment count, and payload size. The receiver can reassemble frames. The code handles errors at every syscall — open, ioctl, mmap, socket, and sendto — and exits gracefully on failure. It runs until SIGINT or SIGTERM is received, then cleanly stops streaming, unmmaps all buffers, and closes all descriptors.

