This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins and the I2C bus. It creates a circular buffer to store temperature readings and writes them to a binary file named `temperature_log.dat`. The program runs indefinitely until it is interrupted by a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal, at which point it flushes the buffer to the log file and releases all resources.

