This code initializes pigpio, sets up the I2C bus and fan pin, reads the ambient and object temperatures from the MLX90614ESF-BAA sensor, logs the readings to a file, and controls the fan based on the object temperature. It handles errors and retries failed I2C reads up to 3 times with a 10 ms delay between attempts. The program also handles SIGINT/SIGTERM signals by closing the I2C handle, turning off the fan, and terminating pigpio.

