This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the I2C bus on the Raspberry Pi. It initializes pigpio, sets up the I2C bus, and sends a continuous measurement command to the Sensirion SDP800-500Pa sensor. It then waits for the measurement to complete, reads the measurement data, calculates the CRC-8 checksum, and checks the checksum. Finally, it reads the temperature and pressure values and prints them to the console. The code also handles errors and uses signal handling to ensure clean shutdown.

