This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the GPIO and I2C buses, and the itimer library to schedule the timer callback. It reads the calibration table from the BMP180 sensor, computes the temperature and pressure using the compensation formulas, stores the readings in a circular buffer, and prints each new reading to stdout. If the temperature exceeds the threshold, it turns on the fan. The code handles errors and cleans up resources on exit.

