This code uses the pigpio library to control a solid-state relay on GPIO17, modulating a resistive heater to maintain a target temperature read from a MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier over the hardware SPI peripheral. It implements a PI controller with anti-windup and a safe maximum duty cycle of 80% to prevent overheating. The code logs temperature and PWM duty cycle to a CSV file with ISO-8601 timestamps. It handles SPI read failure or a MAX31855 fault by immediately setting the heater duty cycle to 0%, logs the error, and continues running. The code also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown — turns off the heater, closes SPI, closes the log file, and terminates pigpio.

