This code uses the pigpio library to read the state of the two Melexis MLX90217 unipolar Hall-effect sensors connected to GPIO 17 and GPIO 27. It implements a state machine that tracks the previous state to determine the direction of rotation. The state machine is protected by a mutex to ensure thread safety. The program uses a condition variable to wait on the main loop, allowing the program to be more efficient and responsive. The program also uses a signal handler to handle SIGINT and SIGTERM signals, ensuring that the log file is flushed and closed and pigpio is terminated cleanly.

