This code initializes the GPIO lines for the four sensors and the LED, and then enters a loop where it polls the lines every 50 ms. If any sensor detects an object, it turns on the LED; otherwise, it turns it off. The program cleanly releases all resources when it exits. The `sigint_handler` function is used to handle the SIGINT signal and close all GPIO lines before exiting.

