This code uses the libgpiod library to monitor the GPIO17 pin on the Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It configures the pin as an input with an internal pull-up and polls it every 100 ms. When a falling edge is detected (i.e., the pin goes from HIGH to LOW), it prints 'FLAME DETECTED' to the console and appends a line to the 'flame_log.txt' file with the current timestamp and 'FLAME DETECTED'. The program handles errors and releases resources on all exit paths. The SIGINT and SIGTERM signals are handled to ensure a clean shutdown.

