This code uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO chip and line on the Raspberry Pi 5. It opens the gpiochip device for GPIO17, requests the line for input direction, and polls the sensor every second. When an obstacle is detected (line reads LOW), it triggers a simulated "self-parking" sequence logged to the console. The code handles errors and releases resources on all exit paths, including the case where the gpiochip or line is unavailable. It also handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) for clean shutdown.

