This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the I2C bus on the Raspberry Pi. It writes the One-Time High-Resolution Mode 2 command to the BH1750FVI light sensor, waits for the maximum conversion time, reads 2 bytes of data, calculates the illuminance, logs the sensor reading to a file, and repeats the process every 5 seconds. The program handles potential I2C write/read errors and sensor-absent paths, and implements clean resource release on all exit paths, including signal handling for SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

