This code initializes the GPIO pins, sets up a timer to fire every 60 seconds, and implements a state machine to control the relays. The state machine tracks the current state of the system (activating, deactivating, or paused) and switches between the relays accordingly. The state changes are logged to the system syslog. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by deactivating all relays and releasing GPIO resources.

