This code uses the pigpio library to control the four relay-controlled lamp actuators on GPIO4, GPIO17, GPIO27, and GPIO22. It reads the lighting schedule from a file named "lighting_schedule.txt" and simulates a sunrise/sunset effect by fading the lamp's brightness over a 30-minute transition. The code handles file read errors, GPIO initialization failures, and invalid schedule entries gracefully. It also uses a signal handler to turn off all relays and release GPIO resources cleanly on exit.

