This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI peripherals. It initializes pigpio, opens a file for writing, maps the file to memory, opens the SPI interface, sets up the SPI, reads the gyro data, calculates and logs the data, writes the data to the file, delays, and repeats the process. If any of the pigpio or file operations fail, it will print an error message and exit. The program will attempt to reinitialize SPI up to 3 times if a read fails.

