This code uses the pigpio library to read data from the ADXL345 accelerometer over I2C. It configures the sensor for ±2g range and enables measurement mode. It then enters a loop where it reads 6 bytes of data every 100 ms, converts the raw values to g-force, and checks for freefall events. When a freefall event is detected, it logs the event to a file and simulates an alarm. The code also checks for I2C errors and handles any errors that occur.

