This code creates a TCP server that listens for incoming connections on port 5000. When a connection is established, it reads the command from the client, converts it to uppercase, and checks if it's either "ON" or "OFF". If it's "ON", it turns on the relay connected to GPIO 18 using the pigpio library. If it's "OFF", it turns off the relay. If it's anything else, it logs an invalid command. The server logs every activation, deactivation, and invalid-command event to a file named "relay_log.txt". The server also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure clean resource release on every exit path.

