This code uses the pigpio library to control a servo motor on GPIO18 and two push buttons on GPIO21 and GPIO22. The servo motor is moved to the locked position (180 degrees) when the lock button is pressed and to the unlocked position (0 degrees) when the unlock button is pressed. The servo position is constrained to the safe range of 500-2500 microseconds. The code also debounces each button press with a 100 ms delay. The code handles initialization failures, prints status messages, and cleanly releases all resources on exit through a SIGINT signal handler.

